  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "The lead was theirs to lose, and they lost it in one inning.",
    "what_this_means": "Texas tied it in the sixth and never trailed again. J.T. Ginn had given them something to work with. Six innings, four runs, seven strikeouts. And the lineup answered early, Henry Bolte driving in three to stake them to a lead through five. Nine RISP at-bats and one run converted. That margin held until the sixth, when everything unraveled at once. Brady Basso and Scott Blewett kept the bleeding contained after that, but the game was already gone. A one-run loss is not a disaster. Losing it after you had it is the recurring thing that matters. They've left runners on in six straight innings now. That's not variance. That's a pattern with consequences.",
    "what_to_watch": "Cody Bradford sports a 2.38 ERA and Texas will trust him against a lineup that struck out seven times last night. Lopez has been sharp lately. 2.04 ERA over his last four starts. But he is the underdog here.",
